### Reasoning

Problem 79 has answer B. Choice B gives `x > -2`; the other choices give `x < -2`.

Problem 80 shows `3m >= -21`. Heath correctly gets `m >= -7`. Marty incorrectly reverses the symbol while dividing by positive 3.

Problem 81 states that `a != 0`. Each result needs a sign case. For `ax < 7`, `x < 7/a` when `a > 0`, and `x > 7/a` when `a < 0`. The same rule applies to the other parts.

Problem 82 is sometimes true. If `a > b`, then `1/a > 1/b` is false when both values are positive and false when both are negative. It is true when `a` is positive and `b` is negative. Values of zero make a reciprocal undefined.
